          @typescript-eslint/no-this-alias  This binding holds `this` under another name. The alias exists to carry the receiver into a nested `function`, which rebinds `this` to something else, and an arrow function closes over `this` directly and needs no carrier. Every later reader now has to establish which of the two names is the real receiver and whether they are still the same object. Use an arrow function and write `this`.
        
